  {
    "chinese": "许多年轻人并非厌恶劳动本身，而是厌恶劳动中被剥夺了意义感的那一部分。",
    "english": "Many young people do not loathe work itself but rather the part of it that has been stripped of meaning.",
    "soundmark": "/ˈmeni jʌŋ ˈpiːpl duː nɒt ləʊð wɜːk ɪtˈself bʌt ˈrɑːðə ðə pɑːt əv ɪt ðæt hæz biːn strɪpt əv ˈmiːnɪŋ/",
    "grammar": [
      {
        "text": "Many young people",
        "role": "S",
        "phonetic": "/ˈmeni jʌŋ ˈpiːpl/",
        "chinese": "许多/年轻的/人们"
      },
      {
        "text": "do not loathe",
        "role": "V",
        "phonetic": "/duː nɒt ləʊð/",
        "chinese": "做/助动词/不"
      },
      {
        "text": "work itself",
        "role": "O",
        "phonetic": "/wɜːk ɪtˈself/",
        "chinese": "工作/它自己"
      },
      {
        "text": "but rather the part of it",
        "role": "O",
        "phonetic": "/bʌt ˈrɑːðə ðə pɑːt əv ɪt/",
        "chinese": "但是/相当/宁愿/这个/那个/部分/…的/它"
      },
      {
        "text": "that has been stripped of meaning",
        "role": "Det",
        "phonetic": "/ðæt hæz biːn strɪpt əv ˈmiːnɪŋ/",
        "chinese": "那个/有/助动词/是（过去分词）/…的/意思是/刻薄的"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "chinese": "工作伦理将劳动视为一种道德义务，而不仅仅是谋生手段。",
    "english": "The work ethic regards labour as a moral obligation, not merely a means of subsistence.",
    "soundmark": "/ðə wɜːk ˈeθɪk rɪˈɡɑːdz ˈleɪbə æz ə ˈmɒrəl ˌɒblɪˈɡeɪʃn, nɒt ˈmɪəli ə miːnz əv səbˈsɪstəns/",
    "grammar": [
      {
